ells has increased to over 22%  these panels generate electricity via a  thin layer of lead halide perovskites  film on top of a coating of conductive  oxide one of the benefits using profs  kites and solar cells is their defect  tolerance unlike silicon cells where  everything has to be aligned perfectly  to work and any damage renders the  entire device unusable perovskite cells  can be simply layered onto a surface and  generate an electric charge making  manufacturing easier and cheaper but  while engineers are hopeful that  perovskite could help to bring down the  price of solar energy they have some  downsides for now the probe skite cells  are small fragile and degrade much  faster than conventional silicon crystal  panels on the order of hours and days  instead of years  if prof Skype can take in light could it  also make it researchers are looking  into improving screens and LEDs using  LED halide perovskites  as quantum dot nano crystals on an LCD  TV screen pixels are made up of three  colors red green and blue tests with  prototype perovskite pixels use a single  kind of light source blue LEDs with  probe skite polymer beads on top to  control the color when the blue light  shines through the beads the color of  the light that makes it through comes  out in a green or red hue while silicon  quantum dot displays are out on the  market already they are very expensive  so like solar panels using halide  perovskites  could bring down the cost of  manufacturing immensely the colors  created by this prof skype prototype  exceeded some television and computer  monitor standards good enough for use in  a future TV even though each of these  uses has some roadblocks to adoption the  massive increase in research and studies  about perovskite means we'll be seeing a  lot of this crystal structure in the  years to come  you
 

